# Implementation skills first

When the user asks for **implementation** — code changes, refactors, fixes, config updates, migrations, new files, dependency installs that alter lockfiles, or other **repo mutations**:

1. In the **first substantive assistant message**, include a **Skills** (or **Skill match**) section **before** making edits or running mutating shell commands.
2. That section must list: matched routing domains (from `cursor-brain/governance/skill-routing-map.yaml`), the specialized skill ids you will follow, and confirm you **read** `.cursor/skills/<id>/SKILL.md` for each (or cite the governor-only read-only exception from `skill_selection_gate`).
3. Use concise bullets; no code edits until this is stated (unless the user already received this in the same turn from a prior message — then one line “Skills unchanged: …” is enough).

Purely **read-only** questions (explain, locate, review with no writes) may skip the Skills section if you state that no mutation is planned.
